WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 1.7 · Strategic Foundations
Strategic objectives: external and internal

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Turn your mission into a few priorities you can actually resource.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
Strategic objectives are the few most important results you will work towards in your first years. They turn your mission into priorities: not the work you do, but what that work should achieve.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
Two kinds, kept apart

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:38.611
External (ESO): The change you want for the people, community or environment you serve. For example: ESO1: Position ourselves as the neighbourhood’s trusted bakery for fresh, affordable bread.

6
00:00:38.611 --> 00:00:50.030
Internal (ISO): What you must build inside to deliver that change: registration, team, money, systems, partners. For example: ISO2: Sales cover our core costs within 18 months.

7
00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.030
Why they matter

8
00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:56.333
1. They decide where your limited time and money go first.

9
00:00:56.333 --> 00:01:03.859
2. They give you a clear way to say no to good ideas that do not fit.

10
00:01:03.859 --> 00:01:10.533
3. Funders, partners and co-founders can see what you are aiming for.

11
00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:11.533
What they guide

12
00:01:11.533 --> 00:01:16.837
1. Your Theory of Change: one pathway for each external objective.

13
00:01:16.837 --> 00:01:23.252
2. Your plans and budget: every activity and cost points to an objective code.

14
00:01:23.252 --> 00:01:29.556
3. Your indicators and reviews: you check progress against each objective.

15
00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:30.556
What to avoid

16
00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:36.600
Too many: keep two to four external and three to five internal.

17
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.793
Writing activities ("run workshops") instead of results.

18
00:01:40.793 --> 00:01:48.207
Inventing numbers you cannot support yet, or leaving an objective without an owner.

19
00:01:48.807 --> 00:01:50.607
You write your objectives with codes, owners and what you will postpone.

20
00:01:50.607 --> 00:01:54.607
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

21
00:01:56.107 --> 00:01:59.207
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
